Description: Estimates synthetic control models while exposing the implementation
    choices that define the synthetic counterfactual: how matching variables are
    constructed, how predictor weights are set, which constraints the donor weights
    satisfy (simplex, lasso, ridge, penalized), whether an intercept is included, and
    which outcome model corrects for bias (OLS, ridge, lasso, augmented synthetic
    control). Runs specification-curve analysis over a grid of these choices
    (Simonsohn, Simmons and Nelson (2020) <doi:10.1038/s41562-020-0912-z>), with
    placebo-in-space and bootstrap inference for single specifications and placebo
    inference for the curve as a whole, and uses 'xgboost' models with SHAP values
    (Lundberg and Lee (2017) <arXiv:1705.07874>) to show which choices drive the
    estimates. Methods follow Abadie, Diamond and Hainmueller (2010)
    <doi:10.1198/jasa.2009.ap08746>, Abadie (2021) <doi:10.1257/jel.20191450>,
    Ben-Michael, Feller and Rothstein (2021) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2021.1929245> and
    Chen and Guestrin (2016) <doi:10.1145/2939672.2939785>.
